From: Akshaj <akshaj@Akshajs-MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 17:12:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(ui): add an Agents tab to the dataset profile

Adds an "Agents" tab next to Lineage on the dataset profile, answering the
question lineage raises but cannot settle: of the consumers downstream, which
ones actually depend on the part you are about to change.

The tab simulates a schema change (drop a column, rename the table, drop the
table) and classifies every downstream agent and skill as breaks / degrades /
unchanged. A skill that reads the table but never names the changed column in
its instruction text comes back unchanged - lineage alone would have flagged it.

Visibility is gated on the `has-agent-consumers` tag, which rides in on
globalTags that the dataset query already fetches, so the tab appears on exactly
the tables an agent fleet reads and costs no extra request.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
